# Checker tasks: what a maker's trade creation, amendment or lifecycle event (Cancellation) leaves for a checker,
# approved or rejected through /checker/tasks. The task kind and the word approval / rejection / self-approval are for
# the reader; the stored task ID picks the task, the call step picks approve or reject. A new kind of task adds its
# name to the alternations below, not a step.

# ── Provisioning ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@When "^checker (approve|reject)s the pending task$"
    Given checker $1 a trade by stored taskId 'createdTaskId'

@Given "^checker (approve|reject) a trade by stored taskId '([^']*)'$"
    Given build json request with path parameter 'taskId' from stored variable '$2' as user 'checker'
    When post to path '/checker/tasks/{taskId}/$1'
    Then response status code is '200'

# ── Build request ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The task of the precondition (createdTaskId).
@When "^(maker|checker) has (?:valid|invalid) data for (?:trade creation|cancellation) (?:approval|rejection|self-approval)$"
    Given build json request with path parameter 'taskId' from stored variable 'createdTaskId' as user '$1'

# The amendment precondition stores its task as createdAmendTaskId. Once it stores it as createdTaskId, amendment joins
# the step above.
@When "^(maker|checker) has (?:valid|invalid) data for amendment (?:approval|rejection|self-approval)$"
    Given build json request with path parameter 'taskId' from stored variable 'createdAmendTaskId' as user '$1'

@When "^checker has valid data for bulk cancellation approval$"
    Given build json request from current scenario with task ids from stored variables 'createdTaskId1' and 'createdTaskId2' as user 'checker'

# ── Make api call ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

@When "^performs the approval for the request$"
    When post to path '/checker/tasks/{taskId}/approve'
    And attach the response body to the report

@When "^performs the rejection for the request$"
    When post to path '/checker/tasks/{taskId}/reject'
    And attach the response body to the report

@When "^performs the bulk approval for the request$"
    When post to path '/checker/tasks/bulk-approve'
    And attach the response body to the report

# ── Assertions ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@Then "^the (?:(?:trade )?creation|amendment|cancellation) (?:approval|rejection) request is processed successfully$"
    Then the 'checker task' should be 'processed' successfully

@Then "^the (?:trade creation|amendment|cancellation) self-approval request is rejected with permission denied$"
    Then failed to 'approve' 'checker task' with status '403'

@Then "^all cancellation tasks should be approved successfully$"
    Then the 'bulk cancellation' should be 'executed' successfully
